WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.166
This paper, from KU Leuven and presented at ICML 2023,

00:00:04.246 --> 00:00:08.412
revisits Kernel Principal Component Analysis
through the lens of convex duality.

00:00:08.492 --> 00:00:12.658
The authors reformulate Kernel PCA as a difference
of convex functions problem,

00:00:12.738 --> 00:00:16.904
then dualize it.

00:00:16.984 --> 00:00:21.150
This single move unlocks three things at once:
gradient-based solvers that avoid the expensive

00:00:21.230 --> 00:00:25.396
cubic singular value decomposition of the Gram matrix,

00:00:25.476 --> 00:00:29.642
a flexible framework that swaps in robust or sparse
objectives through Moreau envelopes,

00:00:29.722 --> 00:00:33.888
and significant speedups on real benchmarks.

00:00:33.968 --> 00:00:38.134
It is a clean example of how the right optimization
viewpoint can extend a classical method

00:00:38.214 --> 00:00:42.380
in several directions simultaneously.
